The problem is when you pray your prayer timeout gets increased
by a random number and there is a small chance that number is
much smaller than you expect.  And there are turns happening
while you create a monster, kill it, and drag it the couple of squares
to the altar.  It can happen that your prayer timeout hit zero while
all this was happening without knowing.  The first and only warning
you get is expecting the offer to be accepted, maybe a reconiliation,
abut seeing a clover instead.

This is why controlling luck so exactly is a pain in the butt big time.
Since your luck went up a random amount, you could look up that
monster's value in the table and guess.  I just keep offering until I
have maxed out to 13 again and go hunting the co-aligned unicorns
that gradually build up on the level that I've been spending so much
time on.



